m proves the base angles are equal (∠ABC = ∠ACB).\n- The theorem also proves the angles under the base are equal (∠CBD = ∠BCE).\n\nThis looks correct. The theorem is about showing the equality of these angles in an isosceles triangle.\n\nSo, the final answer is:\n\n```tactics\ntheorem example_thm (a b c d e : Point) (AB BC AC : Line) (h1 : formTriangle a b c AB BC AC)\n  (h2 : |(a─b)| = |(a─c)|) (h3 : between b a d) (h4 : between c a e)\n  : (∠ b:c:a = ∠ c:b:a) ∧ (∠ d:b:c = ∠ e:c:b) := by sorry\n```\n\n\\boxed{\ntheorem example_thm (a b c d e : Point) (AB BC AC : Line) (h1 : formTriangle a b c AB BC AC)\n  (h2 : |(a─b)| = |(a─c)|) (h3 : between b a d) (h4 : between c a e)\n  : (∠ b:c:a = ∠ c:b:a) ∧ (∠ d:b:c = ∠ e:c:b) := by sorry\n}": 0.12305557933219001}, "cleaned_response": "∀ (a : Point) (b : Point) (c : Point) (d : Point) (e : Point) (AB : Line) (BC : Line) (AC : Line), ((formTriangle a b c AB BC AC) ∧ (|(a─b)| = |(a─c)|) ∧ (between b a d) ∧ (between c a e)) → ((∠ b:c:a = ∠ c:b:a) ∧ (∠ d:b:c = ∠ e:c:b))", "prediction": {"∀ (a : Point) (b : Point) (c : Point) (d : Point) (e : Point) (AB : Line) (BC : Line) (AC : Line), ((formTriangle a b c AB BC AC) ∧ (|(a─b)| = |(a─c)|) ∧ (between b a d) ∧ (between c a e)) → ((∠ b:c:a = ∠ c:b:a) ∧ (∠ d:b:c = ∠ e:c:b))": 1.0}, "groud_truth": "∀ (a b c d e : Point) (AB BC AC : Line), formTriangle a b c AB BC AC ∧ (|(a─b)| = |(a─c)|) ∧ (between a b d) ∧ (between a c e) → (∠ a:b:c = ∠ a:c:b) ∧ (∠ c:b:d = ∠ b:c:e)"}